#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""memory-atlas — graph of the memory layer as a single self-contained HTML.

Topology: emerge (D3-force on canvas, cluster colors, hulls, live-search)
+ Understand-Anything (deterministic [[wikilinks]] + frontmatter parser).
No LLM; viewing needs no server. EDITING (in-browser edit/rename/zone/tags → writeback
to .md) is opt-in via the atlas-serve sidecar — a deliberate break of the old "no server"
claim, active only while the page is served over http. light/work zones come from
membership in MEMORY.md / MEMORY-work.md.

Usage: memory-atlas [--src [NAME=]DIR ...] [--out FILE] [--no-open] [--lang ru|en]
       # --src is repeatable: first root = primary (index-based zones), extra roots
       # (wiki, skills, …) become one zone each; [[links]] resolve same-root first, then globally
       memory-atlas --dump-data -               # print DATA JSON (no render) — pipeline source
       memory-atlas --demo                     # bundled synthetic demo vault
       memory-atlas --data graph.json|-        # render an arbitrary graph (see DATA CONTRACT)
       memory-atlas --self-test

Cross-zone detectors (port of graph-lab multi-canvas: zones = canvases):
  shared_ref            always on — two zones reference the same ghost
  semantic               cosine of embeddings (Ollama loopback, sha-cache)   --no-semantic-cross
  tag_overlap            Jaccard of working tags                            --no-tag-cross
  temporal_proximity     co-modification window 24h                        --no-temporal-cross
  session_co_occurrence  git log co-touched                                 --no-session-cross
  structural_homology    chain-3 motifs (research-tier)                     --structural-cross (opt-in)
Thresholds/top-k — flags with graph-lab defaults (0.75/3 · 0.5/3 · 86400/5 · 1000 · 5000).
--search-vecs — embed int8 embeddings into DATA for client-side semantic search
(works only if OLLAMA_ORIGINS allows file:// — otherwise the client silently degrades).

DATA CONTRACT (for --data and external builders):
{
  "title": str,                    # wordmark in the HUD
  "generated": str, "src": str,
  "host": str,                     # opt.; who built it (browse header + dash-health)
  "zones": {name: [ax, ay]},       # zone anchors in [-1..1]; order = legend order
  "heat": {"label": str, "high": str, "low": str},   # heat-mode caption
  "nodes": [{id,label,desc,type,zone,path,bytes,age_days,mtime?,heat,ghost,light,heavy,orphan,conflict,root?}],
  "edges": [{source,target,kind,w?,score?}],   # kind → EDGE_STYLES in the template; unknown kind = default style
  "roots": {name: abs_dir},         # opt.; multi-root vaults — editor-open resolves node.path against node.root
  "edge_styles": {kind: {c,a,dash?,arrow?,w?}},  # opt.; builder-declared kinds (template merges into EDGE_STYLES)
  "node_metrics": [str],            # opt.; node fields ∈[0,1] → colorMode options (e.g. "forgotten")
  "detectors": [str],              # opt.; which cross-detectors ran (for the status line)
  "vecs": {model,dim,ids,q},       # opt.; int8 embeddings for client-side semantic search
  "browse": {nodes,edges,bodies,stats,types,generated}   # opt.; terminal browse module
}                                    # no browse → browse tab hidden (e.g. --data builders)
node.heat ∈ [0,1], 1 = bright (fresh/hot — polarity is up to the builder).
"""
